# Local-only deployment/migration notes — kept on disk, never tracked
RASPBERRY_PI_MIGRATION.md

# Private deployment assets & internal runbooks — kept on disk (Mac + Pi,
# backed up at pi:~/ChopperBot-private-assets/), never tracked in the
# public repo. The bot reads calendar/*.pdf from the repo root at runtime,
# so these files MUST stay present in the deployment working tree.
calendar/*.pdf
docs/revolucion-z-capabilities.md
docs/deployment.md
docs/environment.md
docs/remote-dev.md
deploy/bin/
deploy/launchd/

# Timestamped .env backups — `pnpm run release --commit` does `git add -A`
.env.bak*

# pnpm's content-addressable store when it is materialized inside the project
# (happens when `pnpm install --store-dir .pnpm-store` or a CI-ish run drops it
# in the repo root). 200 MB of package blobs — `git add -A` must never see it.
.pnpm-store/

